{"step_index":38,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:31:35Z","input_tokens":8199,"cache_read_tokens":88556,"output_tokens":27250,"thinking":"The gear changes appear balanced with an equal number of upshifts and downshifts. This observation aligns with expectations for a closed-loop simulation, mirroring the behavior observed in a typical race lap. Further analysis of the \"gears visited\" data will offer more insights into the simulation's fidelity.\n\n\nThe analysis shows the simulation reaches all 8 gears. Refinement of the downshift and top speed parameters, specifically adjusting the downshift speed delta and the top speed vector, results in RPM values consistently within the target powerband at speeds above 80 km/h. Furthermore, significant curvature values, exceeding 0.008, appear across 25.3% of the lap, coinciding with the apexes and exit kerbs of the simulated track.\n\n\nThe simulation's auditory fidelity is enhanced by incorporating speed-coupled kerb serration frequencies and high-G tire scrub sounds, modulated based on lateral G-forces and track curvature. The next step is to architect the acoustic modeling across 26 camera shots to ensure seamless crossfades, prioritizing phase coherence and cinematic contrast between co-moving and stationary perspectives. A key consideration is preventing abrupt Doppler pitch changes during shot transitions.\n\n\nPer-shot synthesis with 50 ms equal-power overlap-add offers a clean, modular, and mathematically click-free solution to ensure seamless crossfades across all 26 shots. Total audio sample count increases by only 2.7% compared to a single pass. This approach synthesizes each shot on its padded slice, preventing abrupt Doppler pitch changes, and allowing for efficient, targeted acoustic modeling.\n\n\nEach camera shot, regardless of perspective, now integrates its unique Doppler-shifted crankshaft phase, incorporating micro-Doppler effects even for chase and aerial views. Authentic acoustic characteristics, including EQ, formant, reverb, and stereo perspective are applied to each shot, with detailed modeling of specific sounds like the cockpit airbox intake. For example, the onboard views include boosted airbo\n<truncated 8358 bytes>\nut and bark peak. Downshifts incorporate a 58ms rev-match blip, generating a distinct *BAP!* sound. Turbo spooling dynamics are modeled asymmetrically, accounting for MGU-H shaft frequency. Rapid throttle lifts trigger a subtle MGU-H/wastegate flutter.\n\n\nThe core V6 combustion and exhaust harmonic layers are being synthesized, incorporating crankshaft phase with shot Doppler, along with combustion cycle-to-cycle frequency modulation. Harmonic synthesis focuses on key sub/bank orders (1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 4.5), which define the V6's distinctive characteristics. Main firing orders, dynamically weighted by throttle, generate the fundamental frequency and the harmonics' amplitude.\n\n\nTurbulent exhaust gas modulation is now implemented, using bandpass noise amplitude-modulated by valve opening and effective throttle. Asymmetric waveshaping and formant resonator banks are implemented to model exhaust warmth, collector growl, metallic bark, carbon airbox scream, and high-RPM sheen. The static formants are resonating on the car, not Doppler-shifted, as they're not emitting.\n\n\nFixed camera Doppler requires mild resonator frequency shifting, $\\bar{D}_{\\text{shot}}$, for the car's rest frame; this is in addition to per-sample Doppler sweeps.  The MGU-H turbo whistle, at `f_turbo(t) * D_shot(t)`, and subtle gearbox whine are being integrated as separate layers. Shift transients now include a 45 ms ignition-cut pop in the low-mid exhaust, plus a 58ms rev-match blip, both of which are also Doppler-shifted and mixed.\n\n\nUpshifts now trigger a clean \"thump\" and crisp \"crack\" sound effects. Braking generates stochastic \"burble\" sounds at high RPMs with low throttle. Aero wind rush is coupled with vehicle speed, generating a low-frequency buffet, mid-range rush, and high-frequency shear.\n\nA speed-coupled kerb rumble and tire scrub sounds are integrated based on track curvature and lateral G-forces. Fixed camera close pass-bys create a Doppler-swept aerodynamic wake whoosh. Finally, distinct perspective profiles are set per camera view.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nV5 SFX — Telemetry-Synced F1 1.6L V6 Turbo-Hybrid Audio Synthesizer\\n====================================================================\\nReads:\\n  - track_data/silverstone_track.json  (t, v_mps, curv_1pm, s, racing_xy, heading_deg)\\n  - pipeline/v5_anim.py                (read-only AST parse of 26 SHOTS & camera trajectories)\\n\\nWrites:\\n  - renders_v5/sfx_engine_90s.wav      (48 kHz, 16-bit stereo PCM, 2161/24 = 90.0417 s)\\n\\nUsage:\\n  python pipeline/synth_sfx.py\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport ast\\nimport json\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nimport wave\\nfrom math import cos, pi, radians, sin, sqrt\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom scipy import signal\\n\\nPROJ = r\\\"D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\"\\nTRACK_JSON = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"track_data\\\", \\\"silverstone_track.json\\\")\\nANIM_PY = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"pipeline\\\", \\\"v5_anim.py\\\")\\nOUT_WAV = os.path.join(PROJ, \\\"renders_v5\\\", \\\"sfx_engine_90s.wav\\\")\\n\\nSR = 48000\\nFPS = 24\\nSAMPLES_PER_FRAME = SR // FPS  # 2000 exact samples per frame\\nSPEED_OF_SOUND = 343.0         # m/s\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 1. Parse SHOTS & Timeline Constants from pipeline/v5_anim.py (Read-Only AST)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef load_shots_from_anim(anim_path):\\n    with open(anim_path, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        src = f.read()\\n    tree = ast.parse(src, filename=anim_path)\\n    shots = None\\n    total_beats = 162\\n    bpm = 108.0\\n    for node in tree.body:\\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Assign):\\n            for tgt in node.targets:\\n                if isinstance(tgt, ast.Name):\\n                    if tgt.id == \\\"TOTAL_BEATS\\\" and isinstance(node.value, ast.Constant):\\n                        total_beats = int(node.value.value)\\n                    elif tgt.id == \\\"SHOTS\\\":\\n                        safe_ns = {\\\"dict\\\": dict, \\\"True\\\": True, \\\"False\\\": False, \\\"None\\\": None}\\n                        shots = eval(\\n          \n<truncated 42769 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"d:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar\\\\pipeline\\\\synth_sfx.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking","tool_calls"]}
